# Windows batch files must have CRLF line endings. cmd.exe parses them line by
# line and a bare LF can make it lose a `goto` label -- which is not a theoretical
# problem here: ten of these were written with LF, INSTALL-AUTOSTART.bat among
# them, and it uses `goto :found` to pick up the Python path.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Everything else is fine as-is in the working tree.
*.py  text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.md  text eol=lf
*.js  text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
